Subject: Hold the normal MIF and INT operating points for a G955N suspend comparison

The kernel38 platform test reached noirq after reporting MIF 208 MHz and
INT 107 MHz despite the ordinary desktop QoS floor. The Exynos suspend
path pins these operating points through str_freq. Test the already used
421/178 MHz pair on the Korean revision 10 device tree, changing only the
suspend fields. This is a diagnostic for the preceding corruption and
does not establish that the frequency transition caused it.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lte_kor_10.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lte_kor_10.dts
@@ -19,6 +19,16 @@
 #include "exynos8895-dream2lte_gpio_kor_10.dtsi"
 #include "exynos8895-dreamlte_kor-tdmb-00.dtsi"
 #include "exynos8895-dreamlte_fingerprint-sensor_10.dtsi"
+
+
+/* Diagnostic: hold the normal MIF/INT pair through the suspend callbacks. */
+&devfreq_0 {
+	freq_info = <1794000 421000 421000 208000 2093000 1794000>;
+};
+
+&devfreq_1 {
+	freq_info = <667000 178000 178000 107000 667000 667000>;
+};
 
 / {
 	model = "Samsung SM-G955N rev05 board based on EXYNOS8895";
